EXT. SPACE - TIMELESS

!BLACK SCREEN

!FADE IN:

We are drifting through the cosmos. The very edge of the universe seems within reach. No stars inhabit this vast emptiness. Only faintcosmic dust and silence.

JENITER (V.O.)
What's out there? Beyond the edges of the Citadel? Everything I've ever documented has started with one yearning question. I find myself realizing that I've always asked the easy ones. The ones that led me to answers that kept me close to home. But now, I feel compelled to ask a truly difficult question, one that might take me to places I've never been.

Our drifting camera slows, coming to a gentle halt as it hovers at the precipice of the unknown.

Then -

Abruptly, it shifts direction, moving backwards, leaving the edgeness of the deep dark. It glides back through the void. The blackness gives way to an occasional scattering of stars at the far edges of frame.  The camera continues its retreat, past a lone dark system holding as the universe's furthest traveler. The camera speeds slighlty.

More cosmic bodies come into frame, their light piercing the darkness. 

Then faster still. We see more entities, their brilliance growing as the camera accelerates backwards. 

Faster still. Into denser space, revealing an ever-growing tapestry of cosmic wonders. The camera hurtles backwards, the stars stretching into luminous trails as the universe unfolds in all its grandeur.

Then, even faster.  Streaks of light now. Too fast to discern individual stars.

Faster, faster, faster.

Camera rotates 180, moving forward now, celestial bodies rushing past.

A small speck of light emerges and quickly grows brighter and closer, revealing itself as a distant star. The camera zooms past the raging sea of coronas and solar flares, then speeds past, towards the small blue planet orbiting the sun. Camera closes in quickly, then zips into the atmosphere, diving towards the surface, towards the Citadel Heart and its grand spire towering above the city. 

A flash of light ignites as the camera reaches the tip of the grand spire. The brilliance momentarily blinds, then...

CUT TO:

INT. JENITER'S STUDY - DAY

**JENITER (30S)** sits near the glowing hearth of her study, parchment in hand, scribbling.

